    "rationale": "The undiluted readings are flat at about 0.90–0.92 from 6 h to 18 h, right after clean exponential doubling. That pattern looks like the reader saturating rather than real growth stopping. A 10-fold dilution of the 18 h aliquot read 0.3226. That is a dilution-corrected OD of about 3.2, which is about 3.5 times the undiluted reading of 0.91. A reader that responded proportionally would show about 0.09 for a 10-fold dilution of a culture reading 0.9. So the undiluted readings underestimate the biomass. Only one replicate was affordable, so the estimate carries some uncertainty. The 3.2 figure also assumes the diluted reading sits in the linear range."
